        "id": 74674,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-16T21:34:16.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br><blockquote>It is essentially Bloody Knuckles, but better because you don't have to take increased damage, and for 4 damage you can use it for an additional full turn.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nI completely disagree, it is not better than Bloody Knuckles, but at the same time it is not worse. They are two different cards, belonging to two different decks, with the mindset of performing two different goals. So I find it difficult to say that a card is overall better than another.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I agree they are very different, I just wanted to point out that it is better than Bloody Knuckles, which gets more love than Solar Flare gets since the ruling.</p>",
