      {
        "id": 74676,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-16T23:07:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Remember my \"Lamest Games\" thread?&nbsp; By my definition, a game where Ra laid FOTSG on turn 1, Imbued Fire on turn 2 and Solar Flare on turn 3, and then had a free +3 to damage forever, would be a little bit lame.&nbsp; Solar Flare is much cooler post-errata, because you're forced to let it be a short-term boost, which fits the concept of him \"flaring\" briefly with extra power.&nbsp; Although instead of the ruling we got, I might have preferred if the \"deal self 4 psychic damage\" was replaced with \"lose 4 HP\", so that it no longer interacts with Imbued Fire in any case, nor self-triggers Flame Barrier.&nbsp; But either way, it needed something.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Staff + Imbued Fire + Flame Spike + Blazing Tornado, it yields 14 points of damage, which is the same amount as base Ra.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I was assuming you throw the staff for your second power; if you add Blazing Tornado you need an extra card to pull off what's already a four-card combo (the cards aren't too much of a problem thanks to Sunrise, but you still need four card-plays to set it up, and without Argent Adept or an incap hero around, that's three turns of hoping you don't get wiped).&nbsp; But yes it was a little silly for me to mention Conflagration instead of Tornado.</p>",
